#
# The control for `absorbed_undecidable_condition.guard`: a gate that closes with nothing absorbed.
#
# One conjunct, decided, and false. The rule does not apply and there is nothing further to say about
# it, so the run must be silent. A note here would fire on the ordinary case -- most gates in most
# rulesets close because they were meant to -- and a note that common is one nobody reads.
#
rule buckets_named when Name == "nope" {
    Resources.*.Properties.MustBeTrue == true
}
